skill: "vendor-rfp-generator"
sections[3]:
  - "# vendor-rfp-generator\n\nProduce a complete RFP pack: requirements matrix, weighted scorecard and the approval chain that matches the spend band. Use when a vendor need is first scoped, when an incumbent contract approaches renewal with competitive options, or whenever spend above the threshold requires a documented selection process.\n\nOwner: role-procurement-vendor-manager (pod-gna, procurement). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"intake from the requesting role (need, constraints, must-haves); spend-band policy procurement-policy.toon; vendor history from vendor-inventory.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/procurement/rfp-pack.toon with requirements[] (must|nice), scorecard[] weights summing to 100, approval_chain[]; decision memo after scoring\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Run the intake with the requesting role; write the need statement in one paragraph and the constraints as explicit exclusions.\n2. Build the requirements matrix; split into must (pass/fail) and nice (scored) and forbid weighting must-haves - they are gates, not preferences.\n3. Assign scorecard weights to the nice requirements; verify with run_command that weights sum to exactly 100 before anything is sent.\n4. Determine the approval chain from procurement-policy.toon for the estimated spend band; a chain shorter than policy requires a recorded exception.\n5. Check vendor-inventory.toon for incumbents; an incumbent bid is scored on the same scorecard with no incumbency bonus.\n6. Assemble rfp-pack.toon: scope, requirements, scorecard, submission format, deadline and the evaluation process description.\n7. Emit ask_question to the operator listing the approved recipients before distribution; distribution itself is an external action and waits for that confirmation.\n8. Score submissions against the scorecard only; record per-criterion scores with the evidence line that justifies each, not just totals.\n9. Write the decision memo naming the recommended vendor, the runner-up and the negotiation boundaries; route for the approval chain recorded in the pack.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\ndecision memo through approval chain; awarded terms drafted by role-contract-manager.\n"
